WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
[MUSIC]

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.422
Don't be scared to be yourself,

00:00:03.422 --> 00:00:07.829
that's the first thing I will tell
you before applying to Stanford.

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:10.635
Because people think
there's a perfect mold for

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:14.684
an MBA student that they have to follow,
and that's simply not true.

00:00:14.684 --> 00:00:18.390
&gt;&gt; I interviewed with a CEO of
a local medical device company,

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.622
so I was applying out of undergrad.

00:00:20.622 --> 00:00:25.932
So, to go walk into a room and sit
across the table from a CEO of a public

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:30.982
company was a little intimidating
as it would be for most people.

00:00:30.982 --> 00:00:36.496
I think the thing that that stood
out to me from that experience was,

00:00:36.496 --> 00:00:39.805
it was a fairly informal conversation.

00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:41.767
Incredibly down to earth, and

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:46.673
really he was more interested in what I
wanted to do and what my passions were,

00:00:46.673 --> 00:00:51.664
than sort of validating and checking
boxes on, do I fit particular criteria?

00:00:51.664 --> 00:00:55.637
&gt;&gt; There's an overwhelming feeling
when you come to the GSB that you're

00:00:55.637 --> 00:00:56.453
inadequate.

00:00:56.453 --> 00:00:58.145
And you feel it when you're applying,

00:00:58.145 --> 00:01:01.388
you feel it when you're talking to all
the other people that are applying.

00:01:01.388 --> 00:01:06.120
But if there's one thing that I've
learned this year, is that I'm not.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.824
And that maybe I didn't work for
Michelle Obama,

00:01:10.824 --> 00:01:16.093
maybe I didn't cure polio,
but I'm special in my way.

00:01:16.093 --> 00:01:21.200
And if you give yourself that faith
in yourself when you're applying and

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.559
push through the late nights, the edits
of your paper and the crying maybe,

00:01:26.559 --> 00:01:30.935
when you start thinking about
the pressures of writing them.

00:01:30.935 --> 00:01:34.535
I would say, just have faith in
yourself and know if you don't apply,

00:01:34.535 --> 00:01:37.598
then there's definitely not
a chance that you'll get in.

00:01:37.598 --> 00:01:38.530
[MUSIC]

